          "path": "_m/g/c/k/b/talgarreg-wp/memorial-stone-capel-cynon-lla.jpg",
          "filename": "Memorial stone, Capel Cynon, Llandissiliogogo - geograph.org.uk - 612030.jpg",
          "caption": "Memorial stone, Capel Cynon, Llandissiliogogo At a lonely crossroads up on a ridge. From an internet search it appears that Sarnicol is a Bardic name (pen-name), and one of the poet's works is 'Dic Sion Dafydd'. Each mulish fault, save one alone: A quotation from this is Dic somehow got, that prince of fools, A vast vile progeny of mules.  He was a schoolmaster, and was born in a cottage at Capel Cynon, now called Sarnicol.",
          "alt": "Memorial stone, Capel Cynon, Llandissiliogogo At a lonely crossroads up on a ridge. From an internet search it appears that Sarnicol is a Bardic name (pen-name), and one of the poet's works is 'Dic Sion Dafydd'. Each mulish fault, save one alone: A quotation from this is Dic somehow got, that prince of fools, A vast vile progeny of mules.  He was a schoolmaster, and was born in a cottage at Capel Cynon, now called Sarnicol.",
